review_comments:
Can we add a test with an invalid lambda or a invalid method reference? e.g.

```C#
app.MapGet(""/"", () => DoesNotExist());
```

One with a MethodReference:

```
app.MapGet(""/"", GetPersonId);

[Authorize]
public string GetPersonId() => string.Empty;
```

and with a reference to a different source:

```
// Source1 
app.MapGet(""/"", () => PersonHandlers.GetPersonId);
```
Where `PersonHandlers.GetPersonId` is in a separate source file / SyntaxTree

Should this be `DiagnosticSeverity.Information`? I worry that this we don't know all of the possible scenarios that one might want or have an attribute on the method and having false positives is going to be really frustrating to the experience. It would have been a different story if we'd let this bake over 6.0.

Alternatively should we limit this to a well known subset of framework attributes (Authorize, Consumes, Produces, ProducesResponseType)? 

@DamianEdwards  / @davidfowl what do you think?
